`xtask golden`'s usage errors, which stop before it reads the repository or
installs the oracle (exit status 2). `tests/golden/README.md` describes the
commands; the library's unit tests cover their parts.

```console
$ xtask golden help
Record what the frozen Python CLI does, and check an engine against the recordings (tests/golden/README.md); `golden help` lists the options

Usage: cargo xtask golden <COMMAND>

Commands:
  record    Run every case through the oracle and write tests/golden/cases/ and COVERAGE.md. --check-determinism runs every case twice and fails, writing nothing, unless both runs agree byte for byte
  check     Run every case through the engine and compare with the recordings; also checks COVERAGE.md and that no recording is missing or orphaned
  diff      Check, printing every difference in full
  lock      Rewrite tests/golden/oracle-requirements.txt from ORACLE (uv pip compile)
  coverage  Rewrite COVERAGE.md from cases.toml and the recordings
  help      Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help

$ xtask golden
? 2
Record what the frozen Python CLI does, and check an engine against the recordings (tests/golden/README.md); `golden help` lists the options

Usage: cargo xtask golden <COMMAND>
...

$ xtask golden frobnicate
? 2
error: unrecognized subcommand 'frobnicate'

Usage: cargo xtask golden <COMMAND>
...

$ xtask golden record --engine rust
? 2
error: unexpected argument '--engine' found

Usage: cargo xtask golden record [OPTIONS]

For more information, try '--help'.

$ xtask golden check --check-determinism
? 2
error: unexpected argument '--check-determinism' found

Usage: cargo xtask golden check [OPTIONS]
...

$ xtask golden check --jobs many
? 2
error: invalid value 'many' for '--jobs <N>': invalid digit found in string

For more information, try '--help'.

```
